the s p 500 technically fell into a  correction on monday meaning the market  fell by at least 10 percent from its  last high but then we pulled out and  actually closed higher if you've been  watching the stock market to tell you  what's happening you're looking in the  wrong place it's all about bonds i'm  going to explain why the stock market  pulled back how the federal reserve is  involved and what this all means for the  economy and the markets going forward  after the s p 500 touched correction  territory this week everybody wants to  know what happened right the russell  2000 was down 20 from its last record  high and the nasdaq is heading in that  direction too in fact it's having its  worst start to a year since 2008 this is  all about the federal reserve and u.s  interest rates  so late last year the federal reserve  announced it was ending quantitative  easing and beginning quantitative  tightening then on wednesday fed chair  jerome powell doubled down and made it  clear the fed is going full steam ahead  the economy no longer needs this  this  highly accommodative policy that we put  in place so  it's time to stop asset purchases first  and then at the appropriate time  start to shrink the balance sheet at its  december meeting the fed used the term  balance sheet 28 times and we learned  that from the minutes that came out  january 5th that matters because when  the fed shrinks its balance sheet it's  literally pulling money out of the  economy through quantitative easing the  fed has been pushing 120 billion dollars  out into the markets every single month  think about it like this imagine if your  parents have been giving you a thousand  dollars every month in a savings account  and then one day out of the blue they  call you and they say listen the gravy  train's over in three months we're not  putting that thousand dollars a month in  your bank account anymore well  you probably make some life changes  right well that's what's happening with  the stock market  stock traders and investors are making  some life changes with the way they  evaluate stocks are these companies  still worth their lofty valuations if  the fed isn't pumping 120 billion  dollars a month out into the economy the  fed is getting ready to raise u.s  interest rates and that means the cost  of money is going up when the fed raises  rates that makes it more expensive to  borrow it also makes it more attractive  to save now that influences every market  across the board because it changes how  investors value assets if the fed is  going to raise interest rates three  times this year that's going to make it  a lot more difficult and expensive for  companies that aren't currently  generating a profit to be successful and  about one in five large u.s companies  aren't generating a profit right now or  even making enough money to pay off  their debt so a lot of traders out there  are saying yeah yeah yeah we've seen  this before they remember in 2018 when  the fed was raising rates and said they  were going to keep raising rates on  automatic pilot then the market sold off  and the fed reversed course and even cut  interest rates in 2019. well the fed's  gonna have a lot harder time doing that  with inflation at seven percent like it  was in december at least that's what  annetta markowska and a number of other  prominent market watchers think they  think the fed might be stuck with  inflation rising this fast they're not  going to be able to pull back and bail  investors in the market out but watch  out for retail individual investors have  shown they love to buy the dip it's not  about fundamentals for them they've  learned that if stock prices go down the  fed is going to step into the market one  way or another and make sure those stock  prices go right back up but if inflation  doesn't cool  the fed's hands may be tied the fed may  have to decide which is a bigger risk  runaway inflation or a plunging stock  market  what they choose could have huge  implications for the future of the  market and the economy as a whole if you  enjoyed this video hit the like button  and if you're interested in markets and  want to watch and learn more subscribe  to this channel to keep up with my  latest i believe it was president carter  aka jay-z who said i know this game got  valleys and peaks expectation for dips  for precipitation we stack chips  that's all for now see you next time
 

